<IntegrationLayout title="Integrations" description="Account connections operated by Maxfield Allison, with permissions and data handling explained before you connect.">
<p>These are private account connections operated by Maxfield Allison. Each application has a page explaining what it does, what access it asks for, and where the data goes. There is no public signup.</p>
<h2>Available application information</h2>
<p><a href="/integrations/haliphron-calendar-sync">Haliphron Calendar Sync</a> connects authorized Google calendars to a private Nextcloud calendar account. Its page explains writable and read-only calendars and the limits of synchronization.</p>
<h2>Before connecting an account</h2>
<p>Read the application's page and the <a href="/integrations/privacy">integration privacy policy</a>. The <a href="/integrations/terms">terms of use</a> cover these private connections. A future integration needs its own description of access and data use before it can be added here; these pages don't grant permission for other applications.</p>
<p>For access, support, or deletion requests, email <a href="mailto:maxfield.allison@gmail.com" data-umami-event="email-click">maxfield.allison@gmail.com</a>. Please don't send passwords or authorization codes.</p>
</IntegrationLayout>
